READING.
  As a RULE ON ds, the formalised machinery reaches 17-39%, and essentially all of
  that is Theorem 4.8. R3 and R4 need INTEGER ratios at a flank, which is non-generic:
  0.0% of real sets, 0.1% of integer sets. So the flank theorems, though proved and
  axiom-clean, decide almost no difference set on their own.

  LOWER BOUND, stated as such. The U/K calculus needs a period and a clear-opening
  set supplied per family, and the 4,475 census theorems are specific arrangements,
  not a rule on ds. Neither is encodable here, so both are counted as uncovered.

  ExistenceAt8 is NOT satisfied by composing these rules: ~61% of difference sets are
  untouched by any of them. But a lonely instant was found for every uncovered set
  searched -- 3,600 of 3,600 -- and usually at a very early opening.
